00:08:09.000 --> 00:09:30.000
Don't scream, he warned as he forced her into his Pontiac. A passing car's headlights cut through the early morning darkness and swept over her abductor, illuminating his pockmarked face and large eyeglasses. He drove Gemma south along the Seward Highway, where the city streets gave way to snowy fields, forested hills and rugged mountain ranges. Bound by her wrists and ankles with leather shoelaces, Gemma endured a 100-mile long drive, during which she was periodically assaulted and eventually raped. She was relieved when her captor started the long journey back to Anchorage, only for him to perform a U-turn and continue heading south. Why are we going this way? Gemma asked. Her captor told her of a cabin he had taken a woman to a week prior. That's where they were going now. He drove to the expansive Cooper Lake region and turned down a secluded ancillary road that curled up a mountain.
别尖叫，他警告说，同时把她强行塞进他的庞蒂克轿车里。一辆过往汽车的车灯划破了清晨的黑暗，扫过她的绑架者，照亮了他布满痘坑的脸和大眼镜。他带着杰玛沿苏厄德公路向南行驶，那里的城市街道让位于白雪皑皑的田野、长满森林的山丘和崎岖的山脉。杰玛的手腕和脚踝被皮鞋带绑着，忍受了100英里长的车程，期间她断断续续地遭到袭击，最终被强奸。当她的绑架者开始踏上返回安克雷奇的长途跋涉时，她松了一口气，结果他却调头继续向南行驶。我们为什么要走这条路？杰玛问。她的绑架者向她讲述了一座小屋，他一周前曾带一个女人去过那里。他们现在就要去那里。他开车驶往辽阔的库珀湖地区，拐进了一条蜿蜒上山的偏僻小路。

