00:13:17.000 --> 00:14:05.000
Stripped of her jacket and boots, Beth had faced temperatures as low as minus five degrees Fahrenheit in the days she was missing. At that time of year, Anchorage was plunged into a long darkness with less than six hours of light expected per day. Straining to trudge bound and barefoot through three feet of snow, back up the darkened slope, Beth eventually succumbed to the harsh elements and froze to death. In the darkened slope, Beth was found lying on the ground. She was found lying on the ground. In the darkened slope, Beth was found lying on the ground. She was found dead.
贝丝脱掉了夹克和靴子，在失踪的日子里面对着低至华氏零下五度的温度。每年的那个时候，安克雷奇都陷入漫长的黑暗中，预计每天的光照时间不到六小时。贝丝挣扎着被捆绑且赤脚在三英尺深的雪地里艰难跋涉，爬回黑暗的山坡上，最终没能挺过严酷的自然环境，冻死在山坡上。在黑暗的山坡上，人们发现贝丝躺在地上。她被发现躺在地上。在黑暗的山坡上，人们发现贝丝躺在地上。她被发现时已经死亡。

14
00:14:05.000 --> 00:15:06.000
News of what happened to Beth Van Zanten rattled fellow Anchorage teen Gemma Gibbs. She was certain that the man who had abducted and raped her at gunpoint was also responsible for Beth's death. In order to secure her freedom, Gemma had promised never to tell the police what had happened to her. Now she realized that her silence might have enabled her attacker to assault and murder someone else. Compelled by guilt, Gemma went to the authorities and identified her assailant. It was the same man who had attempted to abduct Fiona Kennedy from her lowest drive apartment in November. Now he faced felony charges for two separate crimes, the second he committed while on bail for the first. Yet he managed to secure a deal.
贝丝·范赞滕遭遇的消息震惊了同为安克雷奇少年的杰玛·吉布斯。她确信那个持枪绑架并强奸她的男子也对贝丝的死负有责任。为了保住自由，杰玛曾承诺绝不把发生在她身上的事告诉警方。现在她意识到，她的沉默可能让她的袭击者得以去袭击和谋杀其他人。在内疚感的驱使下，杰玛前往当局指认了她的行凶者。这就是那个11月份试图从最低大道公寓绑架菲奥娜·肯尼迪的同一个男人。现在他面临着两起不同罪行的重罪指控，第二起是他因第一起保释期间犯下的。然而他却设法达成了一项协议。

15
00:15:06.000 --> 00:16:04.000
He pleaded no contest to the charge of assault with a deadly weapon against Fiona. In exchange, charges relating to the abduction and rape of Gemma were dropped. From the prosecution's perspective, there just wasn't enough evidence in that case to secure a conviction. In his sentencing remarks, the judge told the man, I believe you have a serious illness that makes you extremely dangerous. But then he sentenced him to just five years in prison and added, I recommend work release for you as soon as possible so you can pursue your employment and support your family. A model prisoner, the man was released after serving only three months behind bars.
他对针对菲奥娜的持致命武器攻击罪名提出了不予抗辩。作为交换，与绑架和强奸杰玛相关的指控被撤销。从检方的角度来看，该案中根本没有足够的证据来定罪。在量刑陈述中，法官对该男子说：“我相信你患有一种严重的疾病，这让你极度危险。”但随后他判处他仅五年监禁，并补充道：“我建议你尽早获得工作假释，这样你就可以继续就业并养家糊口。”作为一名模范囚犯，该男子在服刑仅仅三个月后就获释了。

16
00:16:04.000 --> 00:17:06.000
When speaking of the outcome, Gemma Gibbs remarked, It was like you're not only raped by the perpetrator, but again by the court. Although there was reasonable suspicion to believe that the same man was involved in the abduction, rape and death of Beth Vanzantin, there was no evidence to support the allegation and that case went cold. Upon his release from prison, the man returned to Anchorage, a city big and busy enough to forget his transgressions. He continued living a normal life while those aware of his history took it with a grain of salt, as the crimes didn't align with the man they knew personally. He remained married, had a second child, moved into a large house, owned three vehicles and started a successful business.
谈到这个结果时，杰玛·吉布斯评论道：“这就像你不仅被作恶者强奸了，还被法庭再次强奸了。”尽管有合理怀疑认为同一名男子参与了贝丝·范赞滕的绑架、强奸和死亡事件，但没有任何证据支持这一指控，该案也随之成了悬案。出狱后，这名男子回到了安克雷奇，一个大到足以让人遗忘他的过错的繁华城市。他继续过着正常的生活，而那些了解他历史的人则对此持保留态度，因为这些罪行与他们个人所认识的那个男人不符。他依然保持着婚姻，有了第二个孩子，搬进了一栋大房子，拥有三辆汽车并创办了一家成功的事业。

17
00:17:06.000 --> 00:18:17.000
For him, it was as though nothing ever happened, but he never changed. In the year after making parole, he lured a 16-year-old girl into his car and drove her around for hours, sexually assaulting her at gunpoint. He warned her not to go to the police or else he would, quote, hunt her down. She complied with his threat. His appetite for dominance and control continued to grow. His stalking grounds primarily encompassed the downtown Anchorage, specifically an area known as the Tenderloin District. Over the years, the construction of the 800-mile-long Trans-Alaska oil pipeline had led to transient laborers rushing to the city. Organized crime followed as drug dealers and dodgy nightclub operators sought to take advantage of the sudden influx of young men with disposable incomes.
对他来说，就好像什么都没发生过一样，但他从未改变。在获得假释后的第二年，他诱骗一名16岁女孩上车并带她兜风数小时，在枪口下对其实施性侵犯。他警告她不要报警，否则他会“追杀她”。她服从了他的威胁。他对统治和控制的渴望继续增长。他的跟踪范围主要包括安克雷奇市中心，特别是被称为田德洛伊区的一个地区。多年来，800英里长的跨阿拉斯加输油管道的建设导致大量临时劳工涌入该市。随后有组织犯罪接踵而至，毒贩和可疑的夜总会经营者试图利用这群拥有可支配收入的年轻男子的突然涌入。

18
00:18:17.000 --> 00:19:09.000
They set up in the Tenderloin District and ran various bars, adult stores and strip clubs. Police were frequently called out to the area to deal with fights and robberies. The women who worked there were particularly vulnerable. Despite being married, the men would prowl the Tenderloin District looking for sex workers. One such occasion occurred in October 1975. He propositioned a dancer at the Kit Kat Club, showing her a wad of cash and asking to have some fun. She agreed. That night, he drove her to the Chugach State Park east of Anchorage and raped her at gunpoint.
他们在田德洛伊区安营扎寨，经营着各种酒吧、成人商店和脱衣舞俱乐部。警方经常被叫到该地区处理打架斗殴和抢劫事件。在那里工作的女性尤其脆弱。尽管已婚，这名男子还是会在田德洛伊区四处寻找性工作者。其中一次发生在1975年10月。他向吉特卡特俱乐部的一名舞女搭讪，向她展示了一叠现金并要求“找点乐子”。她同意了。那天晚上，他把她开车带到安克雷奇东部的库加奇州立公园，并在枪口下强奸了她。

19
00:19:09.000 --> 00:20:09.000
He ultimately released her and, for personal reasons, she chose not to file charges. She did, however, give his vehicle's license plate number to a rape crisis center, which led to his identification. The case was handed over to the Alaska State Troopers, but without the survivor's assistance, their options were limited. A trooper did contact the man's parole officer to inform him of the incident. When confronted, the man admitted to being with the woman, but said her was only ever at date. Then she started demanding money that he refused to pay, which led her to, quote, get mad and holler rape. The parole officer wasn't convinced by his story, but there was nothing more he could do.
他最终释放了她，出于个人原因，她选择不提起指控。不过，她确实将他车辆的车牌号给了一个强情危机中心，这导致了他的身份被确认。案件移交给阿拉斯加州骑警，但在没有幸存者协助的情况下，他们的选择有限。一名骑警确实联系了该男子的假释官，将该事件告知了他。面对质问，该男子承认曾与该女子在一起，但坚称“这只是一次约会”。然后她开始索要他拒绝支付的钱，这导致她“发火并大喊强奸”。假释官对他的故事并不买账，但他也无能为力了。

20
00:20:09.000 --> 00:21:22.000
That was until April the following year. That month, the parole officer appeared in court to testify against the man after he was caught stealing a chainsaw from a superstore. The officer spoke at length about the abduction of the dancer from the Kit Kat Club, while highlighting the defendant's increasingly violent sexual behavior. He went so far as to doubt that the man would cooperate and respond to therapy now, and was of the opinion that he be locked up. Given the Kit Kat Club incident hadn't been verified by the legal process, the presiding judge decided not to take the parole officer's testimony into consideration. He did, however, listen intently when the defendant politely read out a statement to the court. He spoke of his wife and two children, saying they would be made to suffer if he was imprisoned, and he wanted to stay out of jail to support them. He concluded,
直到第二年四月。那个月，假释官出庭作证指控这名男子，此前他因在一家大卖场偷窃链锯被抓。假释官详细讲述了基特卡特俱乐部舞者被绑架的经过，同时强调了被告日益暴力的性行为。他甚至怀疑该男子现在是否还会配合并对治疗做出反应，并认为应该将其关押起来。鉴于基特卡特俱乐部的事件未经法律程序核实，审判长决定不予采纳假释官的证词。不过，当被告礼貌地向法庭宣读一份声明时，他还是仔细聆听了。他谈到了自己的妻子和两个孩子，说如果他被判入狱，他们将会遭受痛苦，他希望留在狱外来养家糊口。他最后总结道，

21
00:21:22.000 --> 00:22:52.000
I want to live a life that's acceptable to society and to myself. After praising the man for speaking so eloquently, the judge sentenced him to five years. The man appealed this decision, and in a written opinion on the case submitted August 1978, the Supreme Court of Alaska said that prior to the chainsaw theft, the man had conducted his life in a normal manner. Quote, He has maintained steady employment, been a good provider, and has earned the reputation of a hard worker and a respectable member of the community. According to the book Fair Game, the defense sought the input of a psychologist, who concluded that their client was markedly disturbed, antisocial, paranoid by nature, and had a relatively weaker ego. In examining his past behaviors to the present day, it was noted that the man's personality had disintegrated to a highly psychotic level, or high schizophrenia scale, high manic scale, and high antisocial scale, with the psychologist adding, quote, There's some narcissism and a magical thinking involved in this also.
我想过一种为社会和自己所接受的生活。法官称赞该男子言辞流畅后，判处了他五年监禁。该男子对这一决定提起上诉，阿拉斯加最高法院在1978年8月提交的一份关于该案的书面意见中表示，在偷窃链锯之前，该男子一直以正常方式生活。引述：他一直保持着稳定的工作，是一个好的顶梁柱，并赢得了努力工作者和社区受人尊敬成员的声誉。根据《公平游戏》一书，辩护方寻求了一位心理学家的意见，该心理学家得出结论，他们的客户明显受到干扰，反社会，天生偏执，且自我意识相对较弱。在审查他从过去到现在的行为时，人们注意到该男子的性格已经瓦解到高度精神病的水平，或者说高精神分裂症量表、高狂躁量表和高反社会量表，心理学家补充道，引述：其中也包含一些自恋和奇幻思维。

22
00:22:52.000 --> 00:24:09.000
The defense scrapped this finding and sourced a second, more desirous opinion. This second doctor diagnosed their client as suffering a variant of a manic depressive disorder known as a bipolar effective disorder, wherein he had poor control over his impulses due to mood and energy upswings. His kleptomania was a result of this disorder. The doctor maintained that the man was responding well to therapy and medication, and felt there would be no more issues if he continued this routine. The appellate judges agreed that the defendant's antisocial behavior was a mental health issue that could be treated. They ordered him to be released on probation at the end of that month. Even though the courts were absolutely convinced that the man would commit additional crimes without the implementation of a medication and therapy regime, administrative blunders meant that he was returned to society without any court ordered guidelines, mandates, or supervision.
辩护方放弃了这一调查结果，并寻找了第二种更合心意的意见。这位第二位医生诊断他们的客户患有一种躁郁症的变体，被称为双相情感障碍，由于情绪和精力的起伏，他对冲动的控制力较差。他的偷窃癖正是这种疾病的结果。这位医生坚称，该男子对治疗和药物反应良好，并认为如果他继续这种常规，就不会再有任何问题。上诉法官同意被告的反社会行为是可以治疗的心理健康问题。他们下令在该月底释放他并进行缓刑。尽管法院绝对相信，如果没有实施药物和治疗方案，该男子将会犯下更多的罪行，但行政失误意味着他重返社会时没有任何法院下令的指导方针、授权或监督。

23
00:24:09.000 --> 00:25:04.000
The following year on Sunday, October 14, 1979, the man sat alone at a club called Ambers in downtown Anchorage with beer in hand, watching a young woman dance on a nearby tabletop. Their eyes met and he asked if they could meet later. A stutter fragmented his words, but his intentions were clear the moment he pulled out a roll of money. The dancer, Judy Russell, accepted his offer. She'd be off in 20 minutes. We'll meet outside, he said. Look for a gold camper. Upon leaving Ambers, Judy spotted a gold-colored pickup truck parked nearby.
第二年，即1979年10月14日星期日，这名男子独自坐在安克雷奇市中心一家名为安伯斯的俱乐部里，手里拿着啤酒，看着一个年轻女子在附近的桌面上跳舞。他们的目光交汇了，他问他们是否可以稍后见面。口吃让他的话语支离破碎，但他掏出一卷钱的那一刻，他的意图已经很明显了。舞者朱迪·拉塞尔接受了他的提议。她20分钟后下班。我们在外面见，他说。找一辆金色的露营车。离开安伯斯后，朱迪发现附近停着一辆金色的皮卡车。

24
00:25:04.000 --> 00:26:04.000
The vehicle, which had a camper attachment in its cargo bed, had seen better days. The man from the club was waiting for her. She followed him into the camper, where he pulled out a .357 Magnum revolver. Judy was forced to strip naked as her hands were bound with snare wire. She was threatened to keep quiet, but Judy screamed constantly. Dreading someone would hear her and contact police, the man leapt out of the camper and rushed to the front of his truck, throwing himself behind the wheel. He sped towards the Glen Highway, hoping to reach the expansive wilderness that framed the northern part of the city before authorities caught up. Little did he realize that behind him, Judy had escaped her restraints.
这辆货厢带有露营车附件的车辆已经破旧不堪。俱乐部的那个人在等她。她跟着他进了露营车，他在那里掏出了一把.357马格南左轮手枪。朱迪被迫脱光衣服，双手被套索线捆绑。她受到威胁要保持安静，但朱迪一直在尖叫。由于害怕有人听到她并联系警察，该男子跳出露营车，冲到卡车前方，扑向方向盘。他加速驶向格伦公路，希望在当局赶到之前到达构筑城市北部边缘的广阔荒野。他没有意识到，在他身后的朱迪已经挣脱了束缚。

25
00:26:04.000 --> 00:27:00.000
When he heard her pounding on the camper's walls, he started to panic. Slamming the brakes, he rushed around his truck to confront her, only to discover that Judy had locked the camper's doors. She quickly crawled into the cab of the truck and locked the doors there too, just as the man appeared outside the driver's side window. It was rolled partway down. The man reached in and grabbed desperately at the door's lock. Judy leant over and wound the window up, trapping his arm. Her sheer terror was matched by his unbridled fury. He smashed the window to free his arm, unlocked the door, grabbed Judy and pulled her bound and naked onto the ground.
当他听到她猛烈捶打露营车壁的声音时，他开始惊慌失措。他猛踩刹车，急忙绕到卡车前去质问她，却发现朱迪已经锁上了露营车的门。她迅速爬进卡车驾驶室，也将门锁上了，就在这时，那个男人出现在驾驶员侧的车窗外。车窗只摇下来了一部分。男人伸手进去，拼命抓着车门锁。朱迪俯身把车窗摇上去，夹住了他的手臂。她极度的恐惧与他肆无忌惮的愤怒交织在一起。他砸碎车窗抽出手臂，打开车门锁，抓住朱迪，把赤身裸体且被绑着的她拖到了地上。

26
00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:53.000
Judy refused to give in. Scrambling to her feet, she broke out in a sprint. Her captor chased her for several blocks before he gave up and returned to his pickup. Lucky for him, Judy wasn't able to identify him to the police, so he got away with it. But that didn't stop him from trying again. Later that same month, he managed to reach the wilderness outside the city as planned. This time, his captive was a 16-year-old girl he had picked up outside a movie theater. He intended to rape her, but when she revealed that she was homeless and hadn't eaten for two days, he let her go.
朱迪拒绝屈服。她跌跌撞撞地站起来，开始狂奔。绑架者追了她好几个街区，直到放弃并返回他的皮卡车。幸运的是，朱迪没能向警方认出他，所以他逃脱了法律的制裁。但这并没有阻止他再次尝试。同年晚些时候，他按照计划成功来到了城市外面的荒野。这一次，他的俘虏是一个他在电影院外接载的16岁女孩。他本打算强奸她，但当她透露自己无家可归且已经两天没吃东西时，他放了她。

27
00:27:53.000 --> 00:29:02.000
This would be a rare and final moment of humanity. Later that fall, he wouldn't be so kind. Annie wandered downtown Anchorage in blue jeans, a sweater, a fur trimmed brown leather jacket and a pair of high-heeled red ankle boots. It was the fall of 1979, and although her ensemble helped ward off the crisp weather that befell Alaska that time of year, it also acted as a work uniform of sorts. Many of the young women employed in Anchorage's infamously rough Tenderloin District wore similar attire. It let male passers-by know that they were sex workers. Annie climbed into the gold pickup truck that was waiting nearby and settled into the passenger seat. Its driver was a white man of average height and build, with short brown hair and a pockmarked face.
这将是他罕见且最后的一丝人性。那年秋天晚些时候，他不会再这么手软了。安妮穿着蓝色牛仔裤、一件毛衣、一件镶毛边的棕色皮夹克和一双高跟红色短靴，在安克雷奇市中心游荡。那是1979年的秋天，尽管她的装扮有助于抵御阿拉斯加那个季节特有的清冷天气，但它某种程度上也充当了一种工作制服。许多在安克雷奇臭名昭著的艰难红灯区工作的年轻女性都穿着类似的服装。这让过往的男性行人知道她们是性工作者。安妮钻进了停在附近的一辆金色皮卡车，并在副驾驶座上坐了下来。驾驶员是一个中等身高和体型的白人男子，留着短棕色头发，脸上满是麻子。

28
00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:56.000
